d work (process-restart recovery). They're mutually exclusive for the same operation. How should reads behave?\",\"header\":\"Read purity\",\"options\":[{\"label\":\"Strictly pure reads\",\"description\":\"Keep touch-suppression: list/show NEVER trigger background work, even on a thread's first touch. Leftover work recovers only when a write/intake/drain touches the thread. Matches your stated goal + SV-01-001 + the new background test. Requires updating Epic-01 TC-1.5 (which currently asserts a read triggers recovery) — a deliberate cross-epic behavior change.\"},{\"label\":\"Pure except first-touch recovery\",\"description\":\"Reads never derive NEW work, but the very first touch of a thread in a process still recovers already-queued leftover work — preserving Epic-01 TC-1.5. Requires relaxing the new background read-only test (added by the prior quick-fix) so it proves read-only-ness without forbidding first-touch recovery. Reads can still cause a provider call on a thread's first open.\"}],\"multiSelect\":false}]}}],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"482bd42d-27c8-4a42-b248-d7570c2506f0\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
