ment 0ms)\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false}}\n260:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01VKMiFeGghebRcSzfZm3rM1\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\timport { DatabaseSync } from \\\"node:sqlite\\\";\\n2\\t\\n3\\t// The one sanctioned below-SDK write in the test suite: inserts a second\\n4\\t// status='open' turn row, a state no public operation can produce (the state\\n5\\t// machine always closes before opening). Columns match the Story 4 turn\\n6\\t// schema in threads/internal/create.ts.\\n7\\texport function corruptTwoOpenTurns(path: string): void {\\n8\\t  const db = new DatabaseSync(path);\\n9\\t  try {\\n10\\t    const row = db\\n11\\t      .prepare(\\\"SELECT MAX(turn_order) AS max_order FROM turns\\\")\\n12\\t      .get() as { max_order: number | bigint | null } | undefined;\\n13\\t    const nextOrder = Number(row?.max_order ?? 0) + 1;\\n14\\t    db.prepare(\\n15\\t      \\\"INSERT INTO turns (turn_id, turn_order, status, opened_at_event_order) VALUES (?, ?, 'open', ?)\\\",\\n16\\t    ).run(`t${nextOrder}`, nextOrder, 0);\\n17\\t  } finally {\\n18\\t    db.close();\\n19\\t  }\\n20\\t}\\n21\\t\\n22\\t// Poison pills for the bounded no-load-everything proof (Epic 04 AC-3.1,\\n23\\t// SV-01-002): overwrite one message's block content — or its derived-form\\n24\\t// metadata — with bytes that are not valid JSON, so any read that *loads* that\\n25\\t// row throws on parse. A bounded list that excludes the message must still\\n26\\t// succeed; a window that includes it must fail. Together that is positive\\n27\\t// proof the out-of-window row was never read, not merely absent from output.\\n28\\tconst NOT_JSON = \\\"{ this is not valid json\\\";\\n29\\t\\n30\\texport function poisonMessageBlockJson(path: string, messageId: string): void {\\n31\\t  const db = new DatabaseSync(path);\\n32\\t  try {\\n33\\t    db.prepare(`UPDATE message_block SET content = ? WHERE message_id = ?`).run(\\n34\\t      NOT_JSON,\\n35\\t      messageId,\\n36\\t    );\\n37\\t  } finally {\\n38\\t    db.close();\\n39\\t  }\\n40\\t}\\n41\\t\\n42\\texport function poisonMessageFormJson(path: string, messageId: string): void {\\n43\\t  const db = new DatabaseSync(path);\\n44\\t  try {\\n45\\t    db.prepare(\\n46\\t      `UPDATE derived_form SET metadata = ?\\n47\\t       WHERE subject_kind = 'message' AND subject_id = ?`,\\n48\\t    ).run(NOT_JSON, messageId);\\n49\\t  } finally {\\n50\\t    db.close();\\n51\\t  }\\n52\\t}\\n53\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"uuid\":\"180962aa-337c-407c-a416-ea9d8d5cab78\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-12T13:25:02.622Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/test/fixtures/corrupt.ts\",\"content\":\"import { DatabaseSync } from \\\"node:sqlite\\\";\\n\\n// The one sanctioned below-SDK write in the test suite: inserts a second\\n// status='open' turn row, a state no public operation can produce (the state\\n// machine always closes before opening). Columns match the Story 4 turn\\n// schema in threads/internal/create.ts.\\nexport function corruptTwoOpenTurns(path: string): void {\\n  const db = new DatabaseSync(path);\\n  try {\\n    const row = db\\n      .prepare(\\\"SELECT MAX(turn_order) AS max_order FROM turns\\\")\\n      .get() as { max_order: number | bigint | null } | undefined;\\n    const nextOrder = Number(row?.max_order ?? 0) + 1;\\n    db.prepare(\\n      \\\"INSERT INTO turns (turn_id, turn_order, status, opened_at_event_order) VALUES (?, ?, 'open', ?)\\\",\\n    ).run(`t${nextOrder}`, nextOrder, 0);\\n  } finally {\\n    db.close();\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// Poison pills for the bounded no-load-everything proof (Epic 04 AC-3.1,\\n// SV-01-002): overwrite one message's block content — or its derived-form\\n// metadata — with bytes that are not valid JSON, so any read that *loads* that\\n// row throws on parse. A bounded list that excludes the message must still\\n// succeed; a window that includes it must fail. Together that is positive\\n// proof the out-of-window row was never read, not merely absent from output.\\nconst NOT_JSON = \\\"{ this is not valid json\\\";\\n\\nexport function poisonMessageBlockJson(path: string, messageId: string): void {\\n  const db = new DatabaseSync(path);\\n  try {\\n    db.prepare(`UPDATE message_block SET content = ? WHERE message_id = ?`).run(\\n      NOT_JSON,\\n      messageId,\\n    );\\n  } finally {\\n    db.close();\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport function poisonMessageFormJson(path: string, messageId: string): void {\\n  const db = new DatabaseSync(path);\\n  try {\\n    db.prepare(\\n      `UPDATE derived_form SET metadata = ?\\n       WHERE subject_kind = 'message' AND subject_id = ?`,\\n    ).run(NOT_JSON, messageId);\\n  } finally {\\n    db.close();\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"numLines\":53,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":53}}}\n283:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"id\":\"msg_01ABvV2QmgDd1abrYB1BqxpP\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01M7MhcYkJdr65PyJM3rpgiS\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts\",\"offset\":70,\"limit\":60},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2492,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":73073,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2492},\"output_tokens\":8,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"uuid\":\"42bbbbbf-790f-47a1-b9b3-57b53df7fee8\",\"request_i