[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"A different test now fails: `work-execution.test.ts` TC-1.5 — background-mode first-touch catch-up drain isn't running. This is the legitimate Epic 01 AC-1.5/1.6 behavior that the touch-suppression work (in the uncommitted changes) appears to have broken. My corrupt.ts edit can't affect this file, so it's from the broader touch-suppression change. Let me investigate the mechanism.\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2248,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":97061,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2248},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"uuid\":\"06177a75-97f1-4088-91bb-c923e89cfc64\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CbySmVP9P4xx45x5HbLan\"}\n783:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":2,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":\", \\\"limit\\\": 75\"}},\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"ddc50a88-f653-4757-a376-8c0d5b0aa86d\"}\n785:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"id\":\"msg_01NuoTrJnDqg6pQqJVcrnDWZ\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01MuxZGjJQwdjdncWCrFzHUM\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/shared/context.ts\",\"offset\":100,\"limit\":75},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2248,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":97061,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2248},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"uuid\":\"b01ba973-7271-45df-8c91-1961fb379cee\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CbySmVP9P4xx45x5HbLan\"}\n791:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01MuxZGjJQwdjdncWCrFzHUM\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"100\\t}\\n101\\t\\n102\\t// The view config for the operation now running: the SDK seam's resolved\\n103\\t// config when one is in scope, undefined for direct domain calls (the\\n104\\t// thread-view surface defaults those itself — see InstanceSeam.view).\\n105\\texport function resolveInstanceViewConfig(): ResolvedViewConfig | undefined {\\n106\\t  return seamStore.getStore()?.view;\\n107\\t}\\n108\\t\\n109\\t// Reads-only operation scope (Epic 03 AC-1.1/AC-2.8): runs fn under the\\n110\\t// current seam with the thread-touch announcement suppressed, so a pure read\\n111\\t// — thread-view pull/status above all — can never schedule a background\\n112\\t// scheduler's first-touch catch-up drain through its openThreadDatabase\\n113\\t// calls (or those of the report surfaces it consumes). Everything else on\\n114\\t// the seam (poke target, view config) carries through unchanged; for a\\n115\\t// direct domain call with no seam in scope the installed scope delegates to\\n116\\t// the below-SDK defaults, minus the touch. Write paths never use this.\\n117\\texport function runWithThreadTouchSuppressed<T>(fn: () => T): T {\\n118\\t  const seam = seamStore.getStore();\\n119\\t  const base: InstanceSeam =\\n120\\t    seam ??\\n121\\t    {\\n122\\t      poke: (threadId) => {\\n123\\t        schedulerPoke?.(threadId);\\n124\\t      },\\n125\\t      touch: (filePath, db) => {\\n126\\t        threadTouch?.(filePath, db);\\n127\\t      },\\n128\\t    };\\n129\\t  return seamStore.run({ ...base, touch: () => {} }, fn);\\n130\\t}\\n131\\t\\n132\\t// Thread-file open announcement (DD-10): openThreadDatabase fires this on\\n133\\t// every open, before any caller transaction begins. Delivers to the SDK seam\\n134\\t// in scope if any (background → first-touch catch-up; manual → no-op), else\\n135\\t// the below-SDK default. The background scheduler learns threadId→filePath\\n136\\t// and runs the first-touch catch-up off this seam.\\n137\\texport function fireThreadTouch(filePath: string, db: DatabaseSync): void {\\n138\\t  const seam = seamStore.getStore();\\n139\\t  if (seam !== undefined) {\\n140\\t    seam.touch(filePath, db);\\n141\\t    return;\\n142\\t  }\\n143\\t  threadTouch?.(filePath, db);\\n144\\t}\\n145\\t\\n146\\t// Transaction owner for operations outside the intake pipeline (mutations,\\n147\\t// repair re-queues, tests of enqueue atomicity): BEGIN IMMEDIATE, run the\\n148\\t// body with a context whose onCommit registrations flush only after COMMIT\\n149\\t// succeeds and drop whole on rollback.\\n150\\texport function runInTransaction<T>(\\n151\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\n152\\t  clock: () => Date,\\n153\\t  threadId: string,\\n154\\t  fn: (ctx: OperationContext) => T,\\n155\\t): T {\\n156\\t  const hooks = createCommitHooks();\\n157\\t  const poke = resolveInstancePoke();\\n158\\t  db.exec(\\\"BEGIN IMMEDIATE;\\\");\\n159\\t  let value: T;\\n160\\t  try {\\n161\\t    value = fn({ db, clock, threadId, onCommit: hooks.register, poke });\\n162\\t    db.exec(\\\"COMMIT;\\\");\\n163\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n164\\t    db.exec(\\\"ROLLBACK;\\\");\\n165\\t    throw cause;\\n166\\t  }\\n167\\t  hooks.flush();\\n168\\t  return value;\\n169\\t}\\n170\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"uuid\":\"4918d4bc-4539-41ff-8ad6-51f1f2163c9d\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-12T13:29:02.931Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/shared/context.ts\",\"content\":\"}\\n\\n// The view config for the operation now running: the SDK seam's resolved\\n// config when one is in scope, undefined for direct domain calls (the\\n// thread-view surface defaults those itself — see InstanceSeam.view).\\nexport function resolveInstanceViewConfig(): ResolvedViewConfig | undefined {\\n  return seamStore.getStore()?.view;\\n}\\n\\n// Reads-only operation scope (Epic 03 AC-1.1/AC-2.8): runs fn under the\\n// current seam with the thread-touch announcement suppressed, so a pure read\\n// — thread-view pull/status above all — can never schedule a background\\n// scheduler's first-touch catch-up drain through its openThreadDatabase\\n// calls (or those of the report surfaces it consumes). Everything else on\\n// the seam (poke target, view config) carries through unchanged; for a\\n// direct domain call with no seam in scope the installed scope delegates to\\n// the below-SDK defaults, minus the touch. Write paths never use this.\\nexport function runWithThreadTouchSuppressed<T>(fn: () => T): T {\\n  const seam = seamStore.getStore();\\n  const base: InstanceSeam =\\n    seam ??\\n    {\\n      poke: (threadId) => {\\n        schedulerPoke?.(threadId);\\n      },\\n      touch: (filePath, db) => {\\n        threadTouch?.(filePath, db);\\n      },\\n    };\\n  return seamStore.run({ ...base, touch: () => {} }, fn);\\n}\\n\\n// Thread-file open announcement (DD-10): openThreadDatabase fires this on\\n// every open, before any caller transaction begins. Delivers to the SDK seam\\n// in scope if any (background → first-touch catch-up; manual → no-op), else\\n// the below-SDK default. The background scheduler learns threadId→filePath\\n// and runs the first-touch catch-up off this seam.\\nexport function fireThreadTouch(filePath: string, db: DatabaseSync): void {\\n  const seam = seamStore.getStore();\\n  if (seam !== undefined) {\\n    seam.touch(filePath, db);\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  threadTouch?.(filePath, db);\\n}\\n\\n// Transaction owner for operations outside the intake pipeline (mutations,\\n// repair re-queues, tests of enqueue atomicity): BEGIN IMMEDIATE, run the\\n// body with a context whose onCommit registrations flush only after COMMIT\\n// succeeds and drop whole on rollback.\\nexport function runInTransaction<T>(\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\n  clock: () => Date,\\n  threadId: string,\\n  fn: (ctx: OperationContext) => T,\\n): T {\\n  const hooks = createCommitHooks();\\n  const poke = resolveInstancePoke();\\n  db.exec(\\\"BEGIN IMMEDIATE;\\\");\\n  let value: T;\\n  try {\\n    value = fn({ db, clock, threadId, onCommit: hooks.register, poke });\\n    db.exec(\\\"COMMIT;\\\");\\n  } catch (cause) {\\n    db.exec(\\\"ROLLBACK;\\\");\\n    throw cause;\\n  }\\n  hooks.flush();\\n  return value;\\n}\\n\",\"numLines\":71,\"startLine\":100,\"totalLines\":170}}}\n793:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":3,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":\", \\\"limit\\\": 50\"}},\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"59ab9806-147a-4468-97fb-1b2c259b97fb\"}\n795:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"id\":\"msg_01NuoTrJnDqg6pQqJVcrnDWZ\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01Fv9NbemjewXp7Yeoc4WWuN\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/test/work-execution.test.ts\",\"offset\":225,\"limit\":50},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2248,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":97061,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2248},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_too