` — whether it routes through the same touch-suppressed module function or wraps it.\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":3668,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":4238,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":143938,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":4238},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"uuid\":\"a74fb140-125f-4d25-ade2-6a3c4ff8a686\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CbyTJ3E9hgdAHnhTTUSss\"}\n1611:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":2,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":\"-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/004-verify\"}},\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"8b21f8a4-e738-4dca-9b90-4e9846e3ddb0\"}\n1616:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"id\":\"msg_01BSi9h5fNSJyyDiK3NswN26\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01EnhXF1JHMY81GbdxGcrz9o\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"python3 -c \\\"\\nimport json\\nd=json.load(open('docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/004-verify.json'))\\nfor f in d['result']['newFindings']:\\n    print('###', f['id'], f['title'])\\n    print(f['evidence'])\\n    print('--- recommendedFix:', f.get('recommendedFix','')[:600])\\n    print()\\n\\\"\",\"description\":\"Read full SV findings evidence and recommended fixes\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":3668,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":4238,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":143938,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":4238},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"uuid\":\"2cc23705-f18d-41f3-ab7f-0e0048e272de\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CbyTJ3E9hgdAHnhTTUSss\"}\n1619:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01EnhXF1JHMY81GbdxGcrz9o\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"### SV-01-001 Message reads can trigger background derivation work\\nTech design DD-6 requires list/show read-only behavior. `messages.listMessages` and `messages.show` call `openThreadDatabase` directly (`packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:262`, `:305`). `openThreadDatabase` fires `fireThreadTouch` on every open (`packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:206-209`), and a background SDK seam routes touch to `scheduler.touch` (`packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:343-350`), which schedules a drain when live work exists (`packages/lhc/src/scheduler.ts:383-395`). I verified the production SDK path with an ad hoc background-SDK scenario: calling `bg.messages.listMessages({filePath},{limit:1})` changed a pending `smoothed_prompt` form to `ready` and recorded `providerCalls: 1`; the same happened for `bg.messages.show({filePath}, 'm1')`.\\n--- recommendedFix: \\n\\n### SV-01-002 Bounded listing still loads all message blocks and forms\\nAC-3.1 requires bounded listing so large threads list without loading everything. `listMessages` reads all message-owned forms before applying bounds via `readMessageForms(db)` (`packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:269`). `readMessages` then selects every row from `message_block` with no WHERE/LIMIT (`packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/store.ts:233-238`) before applying source-order bounds only to the later `message` query (`packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/store.ts:253-271`). A `limit: 1` list therefore still loads/parses full block content and derived forms outside the requested window.\\n--- recommendedFix: \\n\\n### SV-01-003 Configured process gate fails on the Story 1 CLI parity test\\n`pnpm verify` passed, but `pnpm verify-all` failed twice. Both full runs timed out `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` at `messages list mirrors the SDK across default, bounded, include-deleted, and refused options` (`packages/lhc/test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts:98`) after 5932ms and 6627ms against Vitest's 5000ms default. TC-3.4 is the required spawned-CLI parity evidence, so the configured full process gate is not green. A focused `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm exec vitest run test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` passed, but focused evidence does not replace the configured gate.\\n--- recommendedFix:\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"uuid\":\"eb2a31ef-eca2-454a-83bf-5ae0c7d80bd4\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-12T13:36:20.256Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"### SV-01-001 Message reads can trigger background derivation work\\nTech design DD-6 requires list/show read-only behavior. `messages.listMessages` and `messages.show` call `openThreadDatabase` directly (`packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:262`, `:305`). `openThreadDatabase` fires `fireThreadTouch` on every open (`packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:206-209`), and a background SDK seam routes touch to `scheduler.touch` (`packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:343-350`), which schedules a drain when live work exists (`packages/lhc/src/scheduler.ts:383-395`). I verified the production SDK path with an ad hoc background-SDK scenario: calling `bg.messages.listMessages({filePath},{limit:1})` changed a pending `smoothed_prompt` form to `ready` and recorded `providerCalls: 1`; the same happened for `bg.messages.show({filePath}, 'm1')`.\\n--- recommendedFix: \\n\\n### SV-01-002 Bounded listing still loads all message blocks and forms\\nAC-3.1 requires bounded listing so large threads list without loading everything. `listMessages` reads all message-owned forms before applying bounds via `readMessageForms(db)` (`packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:269`). `readMessages` then selects every row from `message_block` with no WHERE/LIMIT (`packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/store.ts:233-238`) before applying source-order bounds only to the later `message` query (`packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/store.ts:253-271`). A `limit: 1` list therefore still loads/parses full block content and derived forms outside the requested window.\\n--- recommendedFix: \\n\\n### SV-01-003 Configured process gate fails on the Story 1 CLI parity test\\n`pnpm verify` passed, but `pnpm verify-all` failed twice. Both full runs timed out `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` at `messages list mirrors the SDK across default, bounded, include-deleted, and refused options` (`packages/lhc/test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts:98`) after 5932ms and 6627ms against Vitest's 5000ms default. TC-3.4 is the required spawned-CLI parity evidence, so the configured full process gate is not green. A focused `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm exec vitest run test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` passed, but focused evidence does not replace the configured gate.\\n--- recommendedFix:\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false}}\n1668:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":1,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\"The verifier's SV-01-001 scenario IS the bg leg added to `messages-read.test.ts`, and the\"}},\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"84b9113b-2aef-47a6-90a0-6bd9329a215a\"}\n1670:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":1,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\"conciliation must be in how the SDK instance wires `messages.listMessages` vs the touch seam. Let me read sdk.ts around the referenced lines \"}},\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"1a1d6f37-baea-401a-bc09-1ef3b66fe995\"}\n1672:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"id\":\"msg_01TAHeEhC4qqFYg1bofB6aQh\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The verifier's SV-01-001 scenario IS the bg leg added to `messages-read.test.ts`, and the verifier never read `work-execution.test.ts` — so it flagged the DD-6 violation unaware of the TC-1.5 conflict. The reconciliation must be in how the SDK instance wires `messages.listMessages` vs the touch seam. Let me read sdk.ts around the referenced lines 343-350 and the messages namespace.\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":7750,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":148176,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":7750},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"uuid\":\"bcaea159-d8dd-417d-84de-a2d1c055bc13\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CbyTM3KSaCTpD9H9uQ4FS\"}\n1680:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":2,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":\", \\\"limit\\\": 160\"}},\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"58581fdb-d057-4b7e-a90f-26f04ad50117\"}\n1682:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"id\":\"msg_01TAHeEhC4qqFYg1bofB6aQh\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_017fy9JV7Fmezyx5gHjYBLjw\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\",\"offset\":240,\"limit\":160},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":7750,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":148176,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":7750},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"uuid\":\"788c6789-5143-4199-b0e7-0a595869a598\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CbyTM3KSaCTpD9H9uQ4FS\"}\n1685:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_017fy9JV7Fmezyx5gHjYBLjw\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"240\\t}\\n241\\t\\n242\\tfunction requirePositive(value: number, name: string): void {\\n243\\t  if (!Number.isFinite(value) || value <= 0) {\\n244\\t    throw new TypeError(`createSdk config: ${name} must be a positive number, got ${value}`);\\n245\\t  }\\n246\\t}\\n247\\t\\n248\\tfunction requireNonNegative(value: number, name: string): void {\\n249\\t  if (!Number.isFinite(value) || value < 0) {\\n250\\t    throw new TypeError(`createSdk config: ${name} must be a non-negative number, got ${value}`);\\n251\\t  }\\n252\\t}\\n253\\t\\n254\\t// Bind a domain surface to one SDK instance's delivery seam (epic-fix-001):\\n255\\t// every operation invoked through sdk.* runs inside runWithInstanceSeam, so\\n256\\t// the poke/touch it triggers deep inside reaches THIS SDK's scheduler\\n257\\t// (background) or a no-op (manual) — never another SDK's. Non-function exports\\n258\\t// (e.g. a domain's workHandlers table) pass through unchanged. The wrapped\\n259\\t// object is the same shape as the namespace, so the public surface type holds.\\n260\\tfunction scopeSurface<T extends object>(surface: T, seam: InstanceSeam): T {\\n261\\t  const scoped: Record<string, unknown> = {};\\n262\\t  for (const key of Object.keys(surface)) {\\n263\\t    const value = (surface as Record<string, unknown>)[key];\\n264\\t    scoped[key] =\\n265\\t      typeof value === \\\"function\\\"\\n266\\t        ? (...args: unknown[]): unknown =>\\n267\\t            runWithInstanceSeam(seam, () => (value as (...a: unknown[]) => unknown)(...args))\\n268\\t        : value;\\n269\\t  }\\n270\\t  return scoped as T;\\n271\\t}\\n272\\t\\n273\\t// The only assembly path: provider, mode, clock, and policy enter here.\\n274\\t// Config mistakes are programmer errors at construction and throw; operating\\n275\\t// failures after construction return OpResults per the error contract.\\n276\\texport function createSdk(config: SdkConfig): Lhc {\\n277\\t  if (config.mode !== \\\"background\\\" && config.mode !== \\\"manual\\\") {\\n278\\t    throw new TypeError(\\n279\\t      `createSdk config: mode must be \\\"background\\\" or \\\"manual\\\", got ${JSON.stringify(config.mode)}`,\\n280\\t    );\\n281\\t  }\\n282\\t  if (config.provider === null || typeof config.provider !== \\\"object\\\") {\\n283\\t    throw new TypeError(\\\"createSdk config: provider must implement DerivationProvider\\\");\\n284\\t  }\\n285\\t  for (const operation of PROVIDER_OPERATIONS) {\\n286\\t    if (typeof config.provider[operation] !== \\\"function\\\") {\\n287\\t      throw new TypeError(`createSdk config: provider is missing operation ${operation}`);\\n288\\t    }\\n289\\t  }\\n290\\t\\n291\\t  const resolved: ResolvedSdkConfig = {\\n292\\t    provider: config.provider,\\n293\\t    mode: config.mode,\\n294\\t    clock: config.clock ?? (() => new Date()),\\n295\\t    retry: config.retry ?? { budget: 3, backoffBaseMs: 5000, backoffCapMs: 60000 },\\n296\\t    lease: config.lease ?? { durationMs: 120000 },\\n297\\t    chunkPolicy:\\n298\\t      config.chunkPolicy ?? { targetProjectedTokens: 2200, maxProjectedTokens: 4400 },\\n299\\t    // Epic 03 (FC-0.2): built-ins merged with user profiles by name, band\\n300\\t    // sums and visibility budgets validated — throws naming the violation.\\n301\\t    view: resolveViewConfig(config.view),\\n302\\t  };\\n303\\t  requirePositive(resolved.retry.budget, \\\"retry.budget\\\");\\n304\\t  requireNonNegative(resolved.retry.backoffBaseMs, \\\"retry.backoffBaseMs\\\");\\n305\\t  requireNonNegative(resolved.retry.backoffCapMs, \\\"retry.backoffCapMs\\\");\\n306\\t  if (resolved.retry.backoffCapMs < resolved.retry.backoffBaseMs) {\\n307\\t    throw new TypeError(\\\"createSdk config: retry.backoffCapMs must be >= retry.backoffBaseMs\\\");\\n308\\t  }\\n309\\t  requirePositive(resolved.lease.durationMs, \\\"lease.durationMs\\\");\\n310\\t  requirePositive(resolved.chunkPolicy.targetProjectedTokens, \\\"chunkPolicy.targetProjectedTokens\\\");\\n311\\t  if (resolved.chunkPolicy.maxProjectedTokens < resolved.chunkPolicy.targetProjectedTokens) {\\n312\\t    throw new TypeError(\\n313\\t      \\\"createSdk config: chunkPolicy.maxProjectedTokens must be >= targetProjectedTokens\\\",\\n314\\t    );\\n315\\t  }\\n316\\t\\n317\\t  // Handler maps merge from per-domain contributions at construction (DD-6).\\n318\\t  // The tables are empty until Stories 2–3 land the real handlers; the\\n319\\t  // assembly mechanics are production code from day one.\\n320\\t  const workHandlers = assembleWorkHandlerMap([\\n321\\t    messagesDomain.workHandlers,\\n322\\t    turnsDomain.workHandlers,\\n323\\t  ]);\\n324\\t\\n325\\t  const drainDeps: DrainDeps = {\\n326\\t    lookupHandler: (kind) => lookupWorkHandler(workHandlers, kind),\\n327\\t    hasAnyHandler: () => Object.keys(workHandlers).length > 0,\\n328\\t    config: resolved,\\n329\\t  };\\n330\\t  const scheduler = createScheduler(resolved.mode, drainDeps);\\n331\\t\\n332\\t  // This SDK's per-instance delivery seam (epic-fix-001). Every operation\\n333\\t  // invoked through the scoped surfaces below runs inside it, so enqueue pokes\\n334\\t  // (DD-5) and thread-file touches (DD-10) reach THIS instance's scheduler in\\n335\\t  // background mode, or a no-op in manual mode — isolated from any other SDK\\n336\\t  // alive in the process. A manual SDK therefore never auto-drains, whatever\\n337\\t  // the construction order, because its operations deliver to the no-op seam,\\n338\\t  // not to whatever a background SDK installed below.\\n339\\t  // The seam also carries this instance's resolved view config (Epic 03,\\n340\\t  // tech design Flow 4): thread-view operations invoked through sdk.* read\\n341\\t  // THIS SDK's profiles/budgets/threshold; below-SDK direct domain calls\\n342\\t  // fall back to the built-in defaults inside the thread-view surface.\\n343\\t  const seam: InstanceSeam =\\n344\\t    resolved.mode === \\\"background\\\"\\n345\\t      ? {\\n346\\t          poke: (threadId) => scheduler.poke(threadId),\\n347\\t          touch: (filePath, db) => scheduler.touch(filePath, db),\\n348\\t          view: resolved.view,\\n349\\t        }\\n350\\t      : { poke: () => {}, touch: () => {}, view: resolved.view };\\n351\\t\\n352\\t  // Background mode also installs the below-SDK default seam so a direct\\n353\\t  // domain call made with no SDK scope — a top-level mutation in the\\n354\\t  // single-background \\\"production path\\\" — still reaches the one installed\\n355\\t  // scheduler. The per-instance scoping above overrides this for every sdk.*\\n356\\t  // call, so the default can never auto-drain a manual SDK's work. Manual mode\\n357\\t  // leaves the default alone (pokes stay no-ops by contract).\\n358\\t  if (resolved.mode === \\\"background\\\") {\\n359\\t    installSchedulerPoke((threadId) => scheduler.poke(threadId));\\n360\\t    setThreadTouch((filePath, db) => scheduler.touch(filePath, db));\\n361\\t  }\\n362\\t\\n363\\t  const work: WorkSurface = {\\n364\\t    drain: (ref, opts) =>\\n365\\t      runWithInstanceSeam(seam, async () => {\\n366\\t        const resolvedRef = await threadsDomain.resolveThreadRef(ref);\\n367\\t        if (!resolvedRef.ok) return resolvedRef;\\n368\\t        return runDrain(resolvedRef.value.filePath, drainDeps, opts);\\n369\\t      }),\\n370\\t  };\\n371\\t\\n372\\t  return {\\n373\\t    threads: threadsDomain,\\n374\\t    intakeStream: scopeSurface(intakeStreamDomain, seam),\\n375\\t    messages: scopeSurface(messagesDomain, seam),\\n376\\t    turns: scopeSurface(turnsDomain, seam),\\n377\\t    threadView: scopeSurface<ThreadViewSurface>(\\n378\\t      {\\n379\\t        pull: threadViewDomain.pull,\\n380\\t        status: threadViewDomain.status,\\n381\\t        compact: threadViewDomain.compact,\\n382\\t        sweep: threadViewDomain.sweep,\\n383\\t        materialize: threadViewDomain.materialize,\\n384\\t      },\\n385\\t      seam,\\n386\\t    ),\\n387\\t    config: resolved,\\n388\\t    scheduler,\\n389\\t    workHandlers,\\n390\\t    lookupWorkHandler: (kind) => lookupWorkHandler(workHandlers, kind),\\n391\\t    work,\\n392\\t    drainSettled: async (ref) => {\\n393\\t      const resolvedRef = await threadsDomain.resolveThreadRef(ref);\\n394\\t      if (!resolvedRef.ok) return; // nothing can be scheduled for an unresolvable ref\\n395\\t      const threadId = peekThreadId(resolvedRef.value.filePath);\\n396\\t      if (threadId === null) return;\\n397\\t      return scheduler.drainSettled(threadId);\\n398\\t    },\\n399\\t  };\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"uuid\":\"bd011366-631f-4f0c-abab-a3b18fd1a464\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-12T13:36:55.330Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\",\"content\":\"}\\n\\nfunction requirePositive(value: number, name: string): void {\\n  if (!Number.isFinite(value) || value <= 0) {\\n    throw new TypeError(`createSdk config: ${name} must be a positive number, got ${value}`);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction requireNonNegative(value: number, name: string): void {\\n  if (!Number.isFinite(value) || value < 0) {\\n    throw new TypeError(`createSdk config: ${name} must be a non-negative number, got ${value}`);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// Bind a domain surface to one SDK instance's delivery seam (epic-fix-001):\\n// every operation invoked through sdk.* runs inside runWithInstanceSeam, so\\n// the poke/touch it triggers deep inside reaches THIS SDK's scheduler\\n// (background) or a no-op (manual) — never another SDK's. Non-function exports\\n// (e.g. a domain's workHandlers table) pass through unchanged. The wrapped\\n// object is the same shape as the namespace, so the public surface type holds.\\nfunction scopeSurface<T extends object>(surface: T, seam: InstanceSeam): T {\\n  const scoped: Record<string, unknown> = {};\\n  for (const key of Object.keys(surface)) {\\n    const value = (surface as Record<string, unknown>)[key];\\n    scoped[key] =\\n      typeof value === \\\"function\\\"\\n        ? (...args: unknown[]): unknown =>\\n            runWithInstanceSeam(seam, () => (value as (...a: unknown[]) => unknown)(...args))\\n        : value;\\n  }\\n  return scoped as T;\\n}\\n\\n// The only assembly path: provider, mode, clock, and policy enter here.\\n// Config mistakes are programmer errors at construction and throw; operating\\n// failures after construction return OpResults per the error contract.\\nexport function createSdk(config: SdkConfig): Lhc {\\n  if (config.mode !== \\\"background\\\" && config.mode !== \\\"manual\\\") {\\n    throw new TypeError(\\n      `createSdk config: mode must be \\\"background\\\" or \\\"manual\\\", got ${JSON.stringify(config.mode)}`,\\n    );\\n  }\\n  if (config.provider === null || typeof config.provider !== \\\"object\\\") {\\n    throw new TypeError(\\\"createSdk config: provider must implement DerivationProvider\\\");\\n  }\\n  for (const operation of PROVIDER_OPERATIONS) {\\n    if (typeof config.provider[operation] !== \\\"function\\\") {\\n      throw new TypeError(`createSdk config: provider is missing operation ${operation}`);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  const resolved: ResolvedSdkConfig = {\\n    provider: config.provider,\\n    mode: config.mode,\\n    clock: config.clock ?? (() => new Date()),\\n    retry: config.retry ?? { budget: 3, backoffBaseMs: 5000, backoffCapMs: 60000 },\\n    lease: config.lease ?? { durationMs: 120000 },\\n    chunkPolicy:\\n      config.chunkPolicy ?? { targetProjectedTokens: 2200, maxProjectedTokens: 4400 },\\n    // Epic 03 (FC-0.2): built-ins merged with user profiles by name, band\\n    // sums and visibility budgets validated — throws naming the violation.\\n    view: resolveViewConfig(config.view),\\n  };\\n  requirePositive(resolved.retry.budget, \\\"retry.budget\\\");\\n  requireNonNegative(resolved.retry.backoffBaseMs, \\\"retry.backoffBaseMs\\\");\\n  requireNonNegative(resolved.retry.backoffCapMs, \\\"retry.backoffCapMs\\\");\\n  if (resolved.retry.backoffCapMs < resolved.retry.backoffBaseMs) {\\n    throw new TypeError(\\\"createSdk config: retry.backoffCapMs must be >= retry.backoffBaseMs\\\");\\n  }\\n  requirePositive(resolved.lease.durationMs, \\\"lease.durationMs\\\");\\n  requirePositive(resolved.chunkPolicy.targetProjectedTokens, \\\"chunkPolicy.targetProjectedTokens\\\");\\n  if (resolved.chunkPolicy.maxProjectedTokens < resolved.chunkPolicy.targetProjectedTokens) {\\n    throw new TypeError(\\n      \\\"createSdk config: chunkPolicy.maxProjectedTokens must be >= targetProjectedTokens\\\",\\n    );\\n  }\\n\\n  // Handler maps merge from per-domain contributions at construction (DD-6).\\n  // The tables are empty until Stories 2–3 land the real handlers; the\\n  // assembly mechanics are production code from day one.\\n  const workHandlers = assembleWorkHandlerMap([\\n    messagesDomain.workHandlers,\\n    turnsDomain.workHandlers,\\n  ]);\\n\\n  const drainDeps: DrainDeps = {\\n    lookupHandler: (kind) => lookupWorkHandler(workHandlers, kind),\\n    hasAnyHandler: () => Object.keys(workHandlers).length > 0,\\n    config: resolved,\\n  };\\n  const scheduler = createScheduler(resolved.mode, drainDeps);\\n\\n  // This SDK's per-instance delivery seam (epic-fix-001). Every operation\\n  // invoked through the scoped surfaces below runs inside it, so enqueue pokes\\n  // (DD-5) and thread-file touches (DD-10) reach THIS instance's scheduler in\\n  // background mode, or a no-op in manual mode — isolated from any other SDK\\n  // alive in the process. A manual SDK therefore never auto-drains, whatever\\n  // the construction order, because its operations deliver to the no-op seam,\\n  // not to whatever a background SDK installed below.\\n  // The seam also carries this instance's resolved view config (Epic 03,\\n  // tech design Flow 4): thread-view operations invoked through sdk.* read\\n  // THIS SDK's profiles/budgets/threshold; below-SDK direct domain calls\\n  // fall back to the built-in defaults inside the thread-view surface.\\n  const seam: InstanceSeam =\\n    resolved.mode === \\\"background\\\"\\n      ? {\\n          poke: (threadId) => scheduler.poke(threadId),\\n          touch: (filePath, db) => scheduler.touch(filePath, db),\\n          view: resolved.view,\\n        }\\n      : { poke: () => {}, touch: () => {}, view: resolved.view };\\n\\n  // Background mode also installs the below-SDK default seam so a direct\\n  // domain call made with no SDK scope — a top-level mutation in the\\n  // single-background \\\"production path\\\" — still reaches the one installed\\n  // scheduler. The per-instance scoping above overrides this for every sdk.*\\n  // call, so the default can never auto-drain a manual SDK's work. Manual mode\\n  // leaves the default alone (pokes stay no-ops by contract).\\n  if (resolved.mode === \\\"background\\\") {\\n    installSchedulerPoke((threadId) => scheduler.poke(threadId));\\n    setThreadTouch((filePath, db) => scheduler.touch(filePath, db));\\n  }\\n\\n  const work: WorkSurface = {\\n    drain: (ref, opts) =>\\n      runWithInstanceSeam(seam, async () => {\\n        const resolvedRef = await threadsDomain.resolveThreadRef(ref);\\n        if (!resolvedRef.ok) return resolvedRef;\\n        return runDrain(resolvedRef.value.filePath, drainDeps, opts);\\n      }),\\n  };\\n\\n  return {\\n    threads: threadsDomain,\\n    intakeStream: scopeSurface(intakeStreamDomain, seam),\\n    messages: scopeSurface(messagesDomain, seam),\\n    turns: scopeSurface(turnsDomain, seam),\\n    threadView: scopeSurface<ThreadViewSurface>(\\n      {\\n        pull: threadViewDomain.pull,\\n        status: threadViewDomain.status,\\n        compact: threadViewDomain.compact,\\n        sweep: threadViewDomain.sweep,\\n        materialize: threadViewDomain.materialize,\\n      },\\n      seam,\\n    ),\\n    config: resolved,\\n    scheduler,\\n    workHandlers,\\n    lookupWorkHandler: (kind) => lookupWorkHandler(workHandlers, kind),\\n    work,\\n    drainSettled: async (ref) => {\\n      const resolvedRef = await threadsDomain.resolveThreadRef(ref);\\n      if (!resolvedRef.ok) return; // nothing can be scheduled for an unresolvable ref\\n      const threadId = peekThreadId(resolvedRef.value.filePath);\\n      if (threadId === null) return;\\n      return scheduler.drainSettled(threadId);\\n    },\\n  };\",\"numLines\":160,\"startLine\":240,\"totalLines\":401}}}\n1791:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":1,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\" TC-1.5's first-touch trigger, or was it recently substituted? And what did the committed HEAD version\"}},\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"f8db9aca-c6ac-44c5-84c4-66e168816b77\"}\n1793:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"id\":\"msg_01B5rQGkxnKVw5dy249VW2cP\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Let me check git history: was `listMessages` always TC-1.5's first-touch trigger, or was it recently substituted? And what did