y exclusive for the same operation. How should reads behave?\",\"header\":\"Read purity\",\"multiSelect\":false,\"options\":[{\"label\":\"Strictly pure reads\",\"description\":\"Keep touch-suppression: list/show NEVER trigger background work, even on a thread's first touch. Leftover work recovers only when a write/intake/drain touches the thread. Matches your stated goal + SV-01-001 + the new background test. Requires updating Epic-01 TC-1.5 (which currently asserts a read triggers recovery) — a deliberate cross-epic behavior change.\"},{\"label\":\"Pure except first-touch recovery\",\"description\":\"Reads never derive NEW work, but the very first touch of a thread in a process still recovers already-queued leftover work — preserving Epic-01 TC-1.5. Requires relaxing the new background read-only test (added by the prior quick-fix) so it proves read-only-ness without forbidding first-touch recovery. Reads can still cause a provider call on a thread's first open.\"}]}]},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1382,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":174758,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":1382},\"output_tokens\":2,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"uuid\":\"2b2cec33-9496-4e30-9bbe-99440a5b5d3b\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CbyTbMPmdcDjxhU6vPBgr\"}\n2508:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":1,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\" which also matches SV-01-001 and the regression test the prior session added. The consequence is that Epic-01 TC-\"}},\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"1fc9018f-1445-4d15-9d1d-3a09a6335fac\"}\n2509:{\"type\":