ernative — **reads pure *except* first-touch rec\"}},\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"ab5e0a1d-7757-487d-a149-5cd91b192ddd\"}\n3044:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":1,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\"overy** — would leave TC-1.5 untouched but means a read *can* still fire a provider call on a thread's very first open (and would require\"}},\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"7b084bf0-1d34-4185-ae56-1bd966e5a92c\"}\n3045:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":1,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\" relaxing the new background read-only test instead). If you'd prefer that direction, say so and I'll switch. I left the pipeline artifacts/imp\"}},\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"5400f2c3-b6d3-4f83-970f-022dd3d20c08\"}\n3046:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":1,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\"l-log and `red-manifest.json` untouched (the configured gates don't consult the manifest; re\"}},\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"1f3f15c0-5be7-4543-bbe2-554fe79c857a\"}\n3048:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"id\":\"msg_012cwiEHNotFxzDyAVCLUrGR\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"All clean — `index.ts` retains the touch-suppression (no experiment debris), temp files removed, and my changes are isolated to two files. Both configured gates are green.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThe Story-1 work was mid-flight: a prior quick-fix session (stalled with an empty result) had applied fixes for the three blocking verifier findings, but the tree didn't pass `verify-all`. I diagnosed and closed the remaining gaps.\\n\\n**What I found and fixed**\\n\\n1. **SV-01-002 — bounded list / out-of-window loading.** The production fix (bounds-before-content in `readMessages`, id-scoped `readMessageForms`) was already in place, but its regression test couldn't run: the `message_block` table carries a v5 expression index `json_extract(content,'$.toolCallId')`, re-evaluated on every write, and `node:sqlite` rejects malformed JSON at write time — so the fixture's poison (`\\\"{ this is not valid json\\\"`) was rejected by SQLite before the read under test ever saw it. I changed `test/fixtures/corrupt.ts`'s `NOT_JSON` to a **JSON5-valid / strict-JSON-invalid** value (`\\\"{'unreadable': true,}\\\"`): the index's JSON5-tolerant `json_extract` stores it, while the production read's strict `JSON.parse` still throws — so the no-load-everything proof is genuinely exercised.\\n\\n2. **SV-01-001 — reads triggering background derivation.** The touch-suppression on `listMessages`/`show` (already present) makes them strictly read-only — the new background read-only leg passes. **But** this collided head-on with an existing **Epic-01 contract test, TC-1.5** (`work-execution.test.ts`, committed/hash-matched), which deliberately asserted that a `listMessages` call *as a thread's first touch* **triggers** background catch-up of stranded work. I proved (empirically, both ways) the two scenarios are observationally identical, so no production logic can satisfy both — one test had to move.\\n\\n   I went with your explicit instruction (\\\"read operations do not trigger background derivation work\\\") → **reads are uniformly pure** (the same model thread-view's `pull`/`status` already follow). I updated TC-1.5 to the new contract: the first-touch read stays pure (leftover rows untouched, no provider call), and recovery happens the moment the process engages via a non-read path (an explicit drain). It still verifies stranded-work recovery; it no longer claims a *read* drives it.\\n\\n3. **SV-01-003 — process-gate timeout.** The 30 000 ms per-test budget on the CLI parity tests was already in place; `verify-all` runs the inspect process suite in ~2 s with no timeout, and SDK/CLI JSON parity (list ×6 cases, show ×3) deep-equals.\\n\\n**Gates rerun (both green):**\\n- `pnpm verify` (story gate): **28 files / 300 tests** — up from the 290/27 baseline, no regression.\\n- `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all` (epic/process gate): **40 files / 337 tests**, process suite ran.\\n\\n**One thing to flag for your call:** resolving SV-01-001 required editing the Epic-01 TC-1.5 test, because strict read-purity and \\\"a read triggers first-touch catch-up\\\" are mutually exclusive. I asked about this but the prompt was dismissed, so I took your task wording at face value (strictly pure reads). The alternative — **reads pure *except* first-touch recovery** — would leave TC-1.5 untouched but means a read *can* still fire a provider call on a thread's very first open (and would require relaxing the new background read-only test instead). If you'd prefer that direction, say so and I'll switch. I left the pipeline artifacts/impl-log and `red-manifest.json` untouched (the configured gates don't consult the manifest; re-recording is the orchestration tooling's job at acceptance).\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2833,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":221920,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2833},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"fc748cdb-c5fb-4e11-a01a-1f0f214d246f\",\"uuid\":\"af1731b9-2a30-4f42-9597-ff0d08bbd4d8\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CbyUPw9Zp8zSNuhpKseur\"}\n3052:{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":1649966,\"duration_ap